  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_006: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted → acc 0.725), evidence is extremely sparse. The most informative next step is a clean single-variable ablation to determine whether the fusion strategy (weighted vs. concat) is a meaningful design choice. Config_021 changes only the fusion from weighted to concat while holding all other settings identical to config_006. If concat outperforms weighted, it reveals that the interaction between modalities benefits from a richer (higher-dimensional) combination, guiding future experiments toward concat-based fusion. If weighted remains better or they are comparable, it tells us fusion strategy is not a major lever and we should prioritize encoder choices (RNA encoder, image encoder) in subsequent experiments. Under the limited budget of 8 remaining experiments, this minimal-change test maximizes information gain per experiment by isolating one critical design dimension without confounding other variables."
}

